From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Techmore <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: add the SMC reboot node

The T8132 SMC node has no reboot child, so the macsmc-reboot MFD cell
has no of_node to bind and every boot logs "Failed to locate of_node".
Restart then falls back to a path that, after a GPU firmware hang, can
land in macOS recovery (seen on the Mac mini M4 on 2026-10-28).

Add the child node, as t8103 and t600x already have. The PMU nvmem cells
(shutdown_flag, boot_stage, boot_error_count, panic_count) are still
missing: the second SPMI bus has no PMU node yet and the M4 offsets are
unknown. The driver still registers and handles reboot and poweroff.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -836,6 +836,10 @@
 			reg-names = "smc", "sram";
 			mboxes = <&smc_mbox>;
 
+			reboot {
+				compatible = "apple,smc-reboot";
+			};
+
 			smc_gpio: gpio {
 				compatible = "apple,smc-gpio";
 				gpio-controller;
-- 
2.50.1
